    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d974">

                <pb facs="1069" n="1057" xml:id="pg1057"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.01/2216: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-16T18:00:00+01:00">March 16, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>859. From L’Heureux. AFHQ has instructed General MacFarlane to ask Badoglio for
                    an explanation of the reasons why without prior notification to the Allied
                    Control Commission the Italian Government took the initiative for exchanging
                    representatives with the Soviets. [L’Heureux.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
